<article class="env-lemma" id="04AJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04AJ">Lemma <span data-tag="04AJ">67.37.5</span>.</a> A smooth morphism of algebraic spaces is locally of finite presentation. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $X \to Y$ be a smooth morphism of algebraic spaces. By definition this means there exists a diagram as in Lemma <a href="/tag/03MJ" data-tag="03MJ">67.22.1</a> with $h$ smooth and surjective vertical arrow $a$. By Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01VE" data-tag="01VE">29.35.8</a> $h$ is locally of finite presentation. Hence $X \to Y$ is locally of finite presentation by definition. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>